        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "Celsius to Fahrenheit"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "The rule F = 9C/5 + 32 is the equation of a straight line with slope 1.8 and y-intercept 32. Every straight line can be written as an equation."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "general form",
          "axes and parallel lines",
          "slope-intercept form",
          "point-slope form",
          "two-point form",
          "intercept form",
          "reading the general form",
          "parallel and perpendicular lines"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "Any first degree equation ax plus by plus c equals 0, with a and b not both zero, represents a straight line.\nThe X axis is y equals 0 and the Y axis is x equals 0; a line parallel to the X axis is y equals b and parallel to the Y axis is x equals c.\nSlope-intercept form: y equals mx plus c, where m is the slope and c is the y-intercept.\nPoint-slope form: y minus y1 equals m times (x minus x1).\nTwo-point form: (y minus y1) over (y2 minus y1) equals (x minus x1) over (x2 minus x1).\nIntercept form: x over a plus y over b equals one, where a and b are the intercepts.\nIn the general form ax plus by plus c equals 0, slope is minus a over b, the x-intercept is minus c over a and the y-intercept is minus c over b.\nA line parallel to ax plus by plus c = 0 is ax plus by plus k = 0; a line perpendicular to it is bx minus ay plus k = 0."
        }
      },
